The '''TIE Advanced x1''', or '''TIE/ad''', was an advanced prototype [[starfighter]] that was part of the [[TIE series|TIE fighter series]] manufactured by [[Sienar Fleet Systems]]. [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] notably flew a [[Darth Vader's TIE Advanced|TIE Advanced x1]].

==Characteristics==
[[File:SalvadorLarrocaTextlessVader2Cover.png|thumb|left|250px|The cockpit of a TIE Advanced x1]]
In designing the [[starfighter]]s of its [[TIE series|TIE fighter series]], [[Sienar Fleet Systems]] drew heavily on the designs of [[Kuat Systems Engineering]] ships such as the [[Alpha-3 Nimbus-class V-wing starfighter|V-wing]] and [[Eta-2 Actis-class light interceptor|Eta-2 interceptor]]. Sienar also experimented with advanced models featuring localized improvements and secret technological breakthroughs, including the [[TIE/ad v1]] prototype, based on Sienar's ''[[Scimitar]]'' [[Star Courier]]. This prototype led to the TIE Advanced x1, which boasted a [[hyperdrive]] and [[deflector shield generator]]. A [[Darth Vader's TIE Advanced|modified early prototype]] of the Advanced x1 line was flown by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] himself. Vader's fighter boasted greater speed and heavier firepower, featuring fixed-mounted twin [[blaster cannon]]s and a [[cluster missile]] launcher.<ref name="USW" />

The x1 was protected by an experimental shield system. A stabilizing field was projected by a supermagnet at the rear of the ship. Deflector energies were deployed from forward and lateral pairs of projector bars. These experimental shield systems would sometimes require last minute tuning, something Vader often did personally.<ref name="SWCVNE">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref> Vader specified a custom cockpit to accommodate [[Darth Vader's armor|his armored suit]], and high-performance solar cells were fitted into the fighter's curved wings.<ref name="USW" /> The ship could also stand and fly under [[water]].<ref name="SW 2020 17">[[Star Wars (2020) 17|''Star Wars'' (2020) 17]]</ref>

==History==
[[File:Rebels_TIE_Advanced_x1_Fathead.png|thumb|left|250px|Darth Vader's prototype TIE Advanced x1]]
As of [[4 BBY]],<ref name="Siege">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Siege of Lothal]]''</ref> the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] owned and operated an experimental<ref name="Darth Vader's TIE Fighter">{{Databank|darth-vader-s-tie-fighter|Darth Vader's TIE Fighter}}</ref> [[Darth Vader's TIE Advanced|modified early prototype]] of the TIE Advanced x1,<ref name="USW" /> which he [[pilot]]ed into the midst of a [[Phoenix Cell|rebel fleet]] in a daring attack that resulted in the destruction of the rebels' [[flagship]], ''[[Phoenix Home]]''.<ref name="Siege" /> He later used it to travel to [[Malachor]] to fight his former [[Padawan]], [[Ahsoka Tano]].<ref name="TotA">{{Rebels|Twilight of the Apprentice}}</ref>

During the [[Battle of Yavin]], Vader again piloted his TIE Advanced x1 to pursue and eliminate the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] fighters attacking the first [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]. He shot down several [[starfighter]]s until his fighter was unexpectedly knocked out of the battle when a [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]] collided with it after a surprise attack by the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]''. After the collision, Vader spun out of control into [[Realspace|space]], thereby escaping the destruction of the Death Star.<ref name="ANH" /> The ship was disabled and left to float in the [[battle station]]'s debris field, though Vader and his ship were later picked up by a [[Gozanti-class cruiser|''Gozanti''-class cruiser]] piloted by [[Ciena Ree]] and [[Berisse Sai]].<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref>

The TIE Advanced only saw a limited production, but it became a favorite of elite units all the same.<ref name="TIE Fighters">{{EncyclopediaCite|TIE Fighters}}</ref> An [[Ace]] of [[Storm Squadron]] flew a TIE Advanced. Other elite Aces from different squadrons also flew the TIE Advanced, becoming a favorite amongst them.<ref name="Storm Ace X-wing">{{FFGXW2|set=TIE Advanced x1 Expansion Pack|cardname=Storm Squadron Ace}}</ref> Pilot [[Maarek Stele]] once flew a TIE Advanced,<ref name="Maarek Stele">{{FFGXW2|set=TIE Advanced x1 Expansion Pack|cardname=Maarek Stele}}</ref> along with others such as [[Juno Eclipse]].<ref name="Pack">{{Asmodee|subdomain=shop|url=x-wing-2nd-ed-5-hot-shots-1-aces-ii-reinforcements-swz97en|text=X-Wing 2nd Ed: Hot Shots & Aces II Reinforcements Pack}}</ref> Following the Battle of Yavin, the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] provided stolen examples of the craft to [[Tatooine rebel cell|Saponza's Gang]].<ref name="Commander" /> Vader continued to fly his TIE Advanced as well.<ref name="Darth Vader 20" /> A TIE series craft, with wings akin to<ref name="Star Wars 8">[[Star Wars (2020) 8|''Star Wars'' (2020) 8]]</ref> an Advanced x1 but without the back design of that fighter,<ref name="ANH" /> was part of Commander [[Ellian Zahra]]'s [[Hunter Fleet]] after the [[Battle of Hoth]]. The fighter took part in the [[battle at Elessia]].<ref name="Star Wars 8" />

At least two TIE Advanced x1s were placed atop hoverpads and shown as part of an Imperial Military parade for [[Empire Day]] on the [[Core Worlds]]<ref name="Star Wars 26">[[Star Wars (2020) 26|''Star Wars'' (2020) 26]]</ref> planet of<ref name="Guide to Batuu">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref> [[Bar'leth]], where new prototypes and officially deployed military hardware were shown off in a galaxy-wide broadcast. However, the [[Rebel Alliance Navy]] took advantage of the broadcast by targeting and [[Unity Day attack|wiping out the parade forces]], ensuring no civilians were harmed but showcasing to the galaxy at large they still posed a threat to the Empire despite the [[Battle of Hoth]].<ref name="Star Wars 26" />

